# Version bumps

Whenever you ship a fix or feature the user can see in the running app, bump the version in the same turn.

1. Patch bump for fixes and small additions (`0.1.2` → `0.1.3`). Minor bump only for larger feature sets.
2. Update all of these together:
   - `package.json` `version`
   - `src/shared/version.ts` `APP_VERSION`
   - `CHANGELOG.md` new section at the top of the release list
   - `README.md` current-version line when it mentions the version
3. Rebuild and update the local Mac app: `npm run pack:mac` (or `npm run build && node scripts/update-mac-app.mjs`).
4. Tell the user the new version number and to quit and reopen (or open) `release/mac-arm64/Pixera Control.app`.

Never leave user-visible changes on the same version string as the previous build. The titlebar / Settings version is how they confirm the update landed.
